  KEY RELATIONSHIP: tiling_count([T]) = H(T) / |Aut(T)|
  (assuming Aut(T) acts freely on Hamiltonian paths)

  If this holds, then tiling count = 7 requires:
    |Aut|=1, H=7: FORBIDDEN (H=7 impossible)
    |Aut|=3, H=21: FORBIDDEN (H=21 impossible)
    |Aut|=5, H=35: possible if H=35 achieved with |Aut|=5
    |Aut|=7, H=49: possible if H=49 achieved with |Aut|=7
    etc.

  And tiling count = 21 requires:
    |Aut|=1, H=21: FORBIDDEN
    |Aut|=3, H=63: possible if H=63 achieved with |Aut|=3
    etc.
